# Line endings.
#
# Windows checks out with CRLF (core.autocrlf=true), and a shell script whose
# shebang ends in \r fails in any POSIX shell except Git Bash, which quietly
# tolerates it:
#
#   ./deploy/deploy.sh: /usr/bin/env^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# Pinning the scripts to LF makes Git Bash, WSL and CI agree. It matters most
# for deploy.sh: a deploy script that runs in one shell and dies in another is
# the sort of difference nobody remembers until a release is in the air.
*.sh text eol=lf
